/* Start here entry for space-3d (demos/lib/starthere/space-3d.js). Generated by tools/activities.py from curriculum/start-here.json:
   edit the data, not this file. demos/lib/starthere.js loads it. */
window.VDStartHere && VDStartHere({"q":"Does pushing harder on a wrench always turn the bolt harder?","q_es":"¿Empujar más fuerte una llave siempre hace girar más el tornillo?","setup":"set=speed~1!ax~0.3!ay~0!az~0!bx~0!by~20!bz~10!showSum~0!showDot~0!showCross~1!labBlind~0!g%3Apresets~torque","do":"<b>Torque on a wrench: τ = r × F</b>: a wrench r = (0.3, 0, 0) m pushed at its end with F = (0, 20, 10) N. Read <b>τ = r × F</b> and <b>|τ|</b>. Now push harder along the handle: under <b>Components</b>, type 15 in the x box of F. Predict, then read <b>|F|</b>, <b>Part of F along r</b>, τ and |τ| again.","do_es":"<b>Torca en una llave: τ = r × F</b>: una llave r = (0.3, 0, 0) m empujada en su extremo con F = (0, 20, 10) N. Lee <b>τ = r × F</b> y <b>|τ|</b>. Ahora empuja más fuerte a lo largo del mango: en <b>Componentes</b>, escribe 15 en el cuadro x de F. Predice, luego lee otra vez <b>|F|</b>, <b>Parte de F a lo largo de r</b>, τ y |τ|.","see":"τ = (0, −3, 6) N·m and |τ| = 6.708 N·m. With F = (15, 20, 10) N, |F| grows from 22.36 N to 26.93 N, but τ stays (0, −3, 6) N·m: the 15 N along the handle does nothing. Only the part of F at right angles to r turns the bolt, |τ| = |r||F| sin θ = 0.3 m × 26.93 N × sin 56.15°. τ itself is at right angles to both r and F, by the right hand rule.","see_es":"τ = (0, −3, 6) N·m y |τ| = 6.708 N·m. Con F = (15, 20, 10) N, |F| crece de 22.36 N a 26.93 N, pero τ se queda en (0, −3, 6) N·m: los 15 N a lo largo del mango no hacen nada. Solo la parte de F perpendicular a r hace girar el tornillo, |τ| = |r||F| sin θ = 0.3 m × 26.93 N × sin 56.15°. τ es perpendicular a r y a F, por la regla de la mano derecha.","explore":[{"setup":"set=speed~1!ax~0.3!ay~0!az~0!bx~0!by~20!bz~10!showSum~0!showDot~0!showCross~1!labBlind~0!g%3Apresets~torque","do":"The same wrench. Under <b>Components</b>, type F = (20, 0, 10) N: the push now leans along the handle, and only its 10 N upward part is across it. Read <b>|F|</b>, <b>Angle θ between them</b>, τ and <b>|τ|</b>. Then press <b>Play</b>, which turns F about the z axis, and watch |τ|.","do_es":"La misma llave. En <b>Componentes</b>, escribe F = (20, 0, 10) N: el empuje ahora se inclina a lo largo del mango, y solo su parte de 10 N hacia arriba queda de través. Lee <b>|F|</b>, <b>Ángulo θ entre ellos</b>, τ y <b>|τ|</b>. Luego presiona <b>Iniciar</b>, que hace girar F alrededor del eje z, y observa |τ|.","see":"|F| is 22.36 N, as at the start, but θ = 26.57° and τ = (0, −3, 0) N·m, |τ| = 3 N·m: only the 10 N at right angles to r counts, 0.3 m × 10 N. As F turns, |τ| swings between 3 N·m and 6.708 N·m and never reaches 0, because the 10 N upward part always stays at right angles to the wrench. The same force can give very different torques.","see_es":"|F| es 22.36 N, como al principio, pero θ = 26.57° y τ = (0, −3, 0) N·m, |τ| = 3 N·m: solo cuentan los 10 N perpendiculares a r, 0.3 m × 10 N. Mientras F gira, |τ| oscila entre 3 N·m y 6.708 N·m y nunca llega a 0, porque la parte de 10 N hacia arriba siempre queda perpendicular a la llave. La misma fuerza puede dar torcas muy distintas."},{"setup":"set=speed~1!ax~2!ay~0!az~1!bx~0!by~0!bz~0.5!showSum~0!showDot~1!showCross~1!labBlind~0!g%3Apresets~lorentz","do":"<b>A proton in a magnetic field: F = qv × B</b>, v = (2, 0, 1) × 10⁵ m/s in B = 0.50 T along z. Read <b>v × B</b> and <b>F = qv × B</b>. Then under <b>Components</b> type 3 in the z box of v, the part of v along B, and read them again.","do_es":"<b>Un protón en un campo magnético: F = qv × B</b>, v = (2, 0, 1) × 10⁵ m/s en B = 0.50 T a lo largo de z. Lee <b>v × B</b> y <b>F = qv × B</b>. Luego en <b>Componentes</b> escribe 3 en el cuadro z de v, la parte de v a lo largo de B, y léelos otra vez.","see":"F = (0, −1.602 × 10⁻¹⁴, 0) N both times, although |v| grows from 2.236 × 10⁵ to 3.606 × 10⁵ m/s. The part of v along B feels no force, so it carries the proton steadily along z while the rest of v turns in a circle: the path is a helix. F is at right angles to v, so the field does no work and the speed never changes.","see_es":"F = (0, −1.602 × 10⁻¹⁴, 0) N las dos veces, aunque |v| crece de 2.236 × 10⁵ a 3.606 × 10⁵ m/s. La parte de v a lo largo de B no siente fuerza, así que lleva al protón de forma constante a lo largo de z mientras el resto de v gira en un círculo: la trayectoria es una hélice. F es perpendicular a v, así que el campo no hace trabajo y la rapidez nunca cambia."},{"setup":"set=speed~1!c1~1.5!c2~70!c3~20!showSurf~1!labBlind~0!g%3AmodeSeg~coord!g%3Apresets~charge","do":"<b>A point charge: V and E depend only on r</b>: 1 nC at the origin, the point P at r = 1.5 m, θ = 70°, φ = 20°. Read <b>V = kq/r</b> and <b>|E| = kq/r²</b>. Drag the θ and φ sliders anywhere, then drag r to 3.","do_es":"<b>Una carga puntual: V y E dependen solo de r</b>: 1 nC en el origen, el punto P en r = 1.5 m, θ = 70°, φ = 20°. Lee <b>V = kq/r</b> y <b>|E| = kq/r²</b>. Arrastra los deslizadores θ y φ a cualquier valor, luego arrastra r a 3.","see":"V = 5.992 V and |E| = 3.994 V/m for every θ and φ, while the rectangular coordinates of P all change: the equipotentials are the spheres r = constant. At r = 3 m, V = 2.996 V, half as much, and |E| = 0.9986 V/m, a quarter. In spherical coordinates this field depends on one coordinate only, which is why the coordinates suit it.","see_es":"V = 5.992 V y |E| = 3.994 V/m para cualquier θ y φ, mientras las coordenadas rectangulares de P cambian todas: las equipotenciales son las esferas r = constante. En r = 3 m, V = 2.996 V, la mitad, y |E| = 0.9986 V/m, la cuarta parte. En coordenadas esféricas este campo depende de una sola coordenada, y por eso esas coordenadas le quedan bien."}]});
